run pnpm run start to get feedback.

do not truncate test output with head or tail. it is always compact enough
 
You can run the test files individually e.g:

```
pnpm test test/adminProposalApproval.spec.ts
```

## Documentation

- Put product requirements and user-facing behavior in `PRODUCT.md`.
- Keep `DEVELOPMENT.md` limited to development setup, tooling, workflows, and verification instructions. Link to `PRODUCT.md` rather than duplicating product requirements.
- Never modify README files (`README.md` or `readme.md`, regardless of filename casing).
- Commit each completed requested change.